[[2047,15,2,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               monitors\nand controls the entire electronic ignition and injection system.</p><p>The system is supplied directly by the battery\nvia a line protected by the maxifuse EFI located on the battery,\nconnector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99 C</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (15/54)\narrives from the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied\ndirectly by the battery at pin 15 of connector A, via a line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition reaches\npin 47 of connector A, via a line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Main injection relay J10 controls the entire system: this is excited by a control signal (earth) received from pin 31 of connector A of control unit M10 and then sends power:</p><ul><li>to pins 16, 32 and 48 of connector A of the control unit,\nthrough the line protected by fuse <strong>F2</strong> of the additional fuse\nbox <strong>B98 A</strong> .</li><li>to air flow meter <strong>K41</strong> , to fuel vapour recovery\nsolenoid <strong>L10</strong> , to variable geometry control solenoid <strong>L15</strong> ,\nto variable valve timing actuator <strong>N76</strong> and lambda probe <strong>K40</strong> ;\n(all these lines are protected by fuse <strong>F2</strong> of <strong>B98 A</strong> ).</li><li>to the fuel injectors <strong>N70</strong> , via the line protected\nby the fuse <strong>F3</strong> , located in the unit <strong>B98 A</strong> ;</li></ul><p>the fuel pump relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition via fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>It is excited by a control signal (earth)\nfrom pin 30 of connector A of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and supplies\npower to fuel pump \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which is earthed through the inertia\nswitch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which cuts off the circuit in the case of a crash\nand so prevents the dangerous spilling of fuel.</p><p>It also supplies power to the ignition coils \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nsignals from the various sensors in order to monitor all engine\noperating parameters.</p><p>Rpm sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K46</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\non engine speed via a frequency signal sent to pins 10 and 59 of\nconnector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . These two signals are very\nlow intensity and are therefore shielded.</p><p>Timing sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K47</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\npin 51 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , receives a reference\nearth from pin 26 of connector B and sends a signal of frequency\ncorresponding to the timing to pin 42 of control unit connector\nB.</p><p>Engine temperature sender unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               riceives\na reference earth from pin 26 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsupplies a signal proportional to the coolant temperature to pin\n25 of control unit connector B. The same sender unit also supplies\ninformation to the temperature gauge and warning light (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Hot lambda probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides control\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               with information on the correct composition of the\nair-fuel mixture. The signal is sent to pin 23 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhile pin 55 provides a reference earth signal. Probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nheated by a resistor in order to ensure it works efficiently even\nwhen cold. The resistor is supplied by relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and receives\nan earth signal from pin 34 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Knock sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\non knock status via a frequency signal sent to pin 22 of connector\nB of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives a reference earth from\npin 54 of connector B. The signals are very low intensity and are\ntherefore shielded.</p><p>Air flow meter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (supplied from\nrelay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) receives a reference voltage from pin 63 of connector\nA and sends pin 57 of connector A a signal proportional to air flow. \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              also contains an air temperature sensor: the sensor reference earth\nis supplied by pin 25 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while an air\ntemperature signal is received by pin 54 of connector A.</p><p>Accelerator pedal K55 is fitted with two\nbuilt-in potentiometers (a main one and a safety back-up). The first\nreceives power and earth from pins 56 and 24 respectively of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a corresponding signal to pin 8 of the\nsame connector. The second receives power and earth from pins 7\nand 25 respectively of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a corresponding\nsignal to pin 40 of connector A.</p><p>Pin 274 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              receives\nthe signal coming from the brake lights switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , with\nthe supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3233830\">E2021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the opening\nof individual injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via duty cycle signals produced\nby pins 19 (cyl.  1), 52 (cyl. 2), 35 (cyl. 3) and 3 (cyl. 4) of\nconnector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive a power supply\nto enable opening from main relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also controls coils \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via\ncontrol signals (earth) for the coil primary windings, while the\nsecondary winding sends a pulse to the spark plugs: from pins 16\nand 14 of connector B for cylinder pair 1-4 and from pins 30 and\n31 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               for cylinders 2-3.</p><p>The primary windings of the coils \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive\na signal to enable opening from main relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Throttle body actuator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N75</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is fitted\nwith two built-in potentiometers connected in parallel: they control\nthrottle opening via a stepper motor.</p><p>The motor receives information from pins\n17 - 49 and 1 - 33 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . Pin 58 of connector\nB sends a power supply to both potentiometers, pin 26 supplies an\nearth signal to the potentiometers, while pins 24 and 41 of the same\nconnector receive signals from the throttle body actuator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N75</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Fuel vapour recovery solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               allows\nfuel vapours to pass through to the engine intake where they join\nthe mixture entering the combustion chamber. Valve \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , supplied\nby main relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , is opened by the control unit when the engine\nis under load via a duty-cycle signal from pin 5 of connector B\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Variable geometry solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\ncontrolled from pin 4 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Variable valve timing system \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N76</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls\nintake advance mechanically: it is controlled by pin 36 of control\nunit connector B.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe ALFA ROMEO CODE control unit via a line from pin 3 of connector\nA  (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234721\">E7010</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-test\nsystem that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nthis receives signals from pin 52 of connector A of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through\nthe tester line.  The self-test system also produces the signal\nfor the &quot;injection failure&quot; warning light in the instrument \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which comes from pin 46 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives an ignition-controlled\nsupply (INT) at pin 15 of connector A from the line protected by\nfuse F4 of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; when this earth\nsignal is received, the &quot;injection failure&quot; warning light\ncomes on.</p><p>The speedometer signal (vehicle speed) reaches\npin 44 of connector A of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234310\">E4021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends out a signal\nproportional to engine rpm (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234270\">E4020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              )\nfrom pin 35 of connector A.</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe air conditioning system via pins 6 and 13 of connector A. This\nallows engine idling speed to be adjusted to increased engine load\nwhenever the compressor is activated, or to turn off the compressor in\nthe case of high speeds or high engine loads (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234652\">E6021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>The control unit also controls the engine\ncooling system: pins 9, 41, 50 and 62 of connector A control activation\nof the relevant fan  (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234439\">E5020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe gearbox control unit (SELESPEED) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M54</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               via pins 12 and\n29 of connector A (&quot;CAN&quot; lines). (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234832\">E7050</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              )</p>"]]